From 49d275daa84e0c676d99aebc562f3601520a7788 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yusheng Peng <jiusi0519@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 19:57:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(gateway): executor liveness probes and mdds subnet
 pinning

GW-04 investigation support and route determinism:

- per-bridge 2s alive timer on the shared single-threaded executor plus
  a >20ms slow-write warning: distinguishes 'executor wedged' from
  'cyclone stopped delivering' in post-mortem logs (proved the executor
  healthy during the GW-04 freeze, disproving the blocking-write theory)
- new gateway config key mdds_udp_peer_allow (comma-separated IPv4
  CIDRs) forwarded to mdds ParticipantConfig::udp_peer_allow_cidrs;
  multi-homed gateways pin board-to-board bulk traffic to the wired link
- rmw_mdds: MDDS_UDP_PEER_ALLOW env var, same plumbing as MDDS_TRANSPORT
- test_status.md: record platform-level ros2 action send_goal hang
  (reproduces with cyclone loopback too) and hidden-topic CLI semantics
