+/// The MddsEvent whose callback is currently executing on THIS thread. All
+/// rmw_mdds event callbacks use one process-wide strand (below), rather than
+/// a strand per rmw_context. Consequently, a callback in context A may safely
+/// clear or replace an event callback in context B without draining B: B can
+/// only be queued behind this callback and must re-check its generation before
+/// dereferencing the retired user_data. The process-wide scope is important:
+/// a context-local strand allowed an A callback to skip B's drain while B's
+/// old callback was executing concurrently.
+thread_local MddsEvent * t_delivering_event = nullptr;
