+// typesupports, following the same wire conventions as rmw_cyclonedds_cpp:
+// 4-byte encapsulation header, field alignment relative to the end of the
+// header, strings length-prefixed including their NUL terminator, wstrings
+// length-prefixed without terminator and one 32-bit word per character.
+//
+// Everything here is internal to serdes.cpp; it lives in a header only so
+// that test/test_serdes.cpp can exercise it directly. Not installed.
+//
+// Decode-side hardening against malicious payloads — every check runs BEFORE
+// the allocation it guards:
+// - each wire length prefix is validated against the minimum payload bytes
+//   one counted item must occupy (CdrReader::check_count with a per-element
+//   minimum wire width), so a forged sequence<uint64>/sequence<double>
+//   prefix cannot amplify a heap allocation 8x and nested sequences cannot
+//   compound that amplification;
+// - IDL string/wstring bounds are enforced right after the length prefix is
+//   read, before the destination buffer is allocated;
+// - a per-message allocation budget caps the total heap growth one payload
+//   may drive, as a backstop for the amplification a per-count byte check
+//   fundamentally cannot catch (e.g. sequences of near-empty messages, whose
